{"name":"Racing Red","hex":"#c21727","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"racing","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The sport of competing in races."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of race"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/racing"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rosso corsa","blocks":[{"text":"Rosso corsa is the red international motor racing colour of cars entered by teams from Italy."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rosso_corsa"},{"title":"Racing","blocks":[{"text":"In sports, racing is a competition of speed, in which competitors try to complete a given task in the shortest amount of time. Typically this involves traversing some distance, but it can be any other task involving speed to reach a specific goal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Rowing_at_the_2012_Summer_Olympics_9240_Mens_lightweight_coxless_four_-_Heat_2_-_GBR_CZE.jpg/330px-Rowing_at_the_2012_Summer_Olympics_9240_Mens_lightweight_coxless_four_-_Heat_2_-_GBR_CZE.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Racing"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/FoS20162016_0625_095227AA_%2827826218151%29.jpg/120px-FoS20162016_0625_095227AA_%2827826218151%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/FoS20162016_0625_095227AA_%2827826218151%29.jpg/250px-FoS20162016_0625_095227AA_%2827826218151%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/63/FoS20162016_0625_095227AA_%2827826218151%29.jpg/120px-FoS20162016_0625_095227AA_%2827826218151%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFoS20162016_0625_095227AA_(27826218151).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg/120px-1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg/250px-1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/41/1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg/120px-1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A1925_Itala_Tipo_11.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia